{"title":"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Using_Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Using Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ike and Mike go into a sandwich shop with a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad21cce05f516e4e69160edb4e98d2f33100215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$30.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> to spend. Sandwiches cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548449edef6f356497f86f09cf9560103142d19e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$4.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> each and soft drinks cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c78cd0de09afc053c5a7244659a936a9c59df2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> each. Ike and Mike plan to buy as many sandwiches as they can,\nand use any remaining money to buy soft drinks. Counting both sandwiches and soft drinks, how\nmany items will they buy?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/a/b5aa255603d2b9691f4db8415c51524b7f034238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }6\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }7\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }8\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }9\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"362\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that the sandwiches cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e524453b36a3214fc103cdedc21a90d2074ca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" /> dollars. Guessing will bring us to multiplying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e524453b36a3214fc103cdedc21a90d2074ca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" /> by 6, which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce8e06423659e5312d61a07247f7b8673da8d3cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27.00$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. Since they can spend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/cedd3173d554b9f605c3e994f5d253eda10a4b6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30.00$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> they have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollars left. Since soft drinks cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/078860bc3c75731e529cf5127116af83716a0631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" /> dollar each, they can buy 3 soft drinks, which makes them spend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/cedd3173d554b9f605c3e994f5d253eda10a4b6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30.00$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />  Since they bought 6 sandwiches and 3 soft drinks, they bought a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> items. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8a806de3bdf2c155767a6042823fe88c689ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>- SBose\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Using_Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Using_Algebra)\">Solution 2 (Using Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Using Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of sandwiches and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of sodas. We have to satisfy the equation of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c8e776fe1543c6342e6785f6d11ae6e2cc34420.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4.50s+d=30\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />\nIn the question, it states that Ike and Mike buys as many sandwiches as possible. \nSo, we drop the number of sodas for a while.\nWe have: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d6198396c20242ac66a7388a6a2e3a8f13787d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 4.50s&amp;=30 \\\\ s&amp;=\\frac{30}{4.5} \\\\ s&amp;=6R3 \\end{align*}\" width=\"96\" height=\"82\" />\nWe don't want a remainder so the maximum number of sandwiches is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nThe total money spent is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65a1286edcbe55be5d4c51e15b94941835aed27c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot 4.50=27$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"97\" height=\"13\" />.\nThe number of dollar left to spent on sodas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff4694a50a8ac2d348dd28c24a10b74e22f6cc0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-27=3$\" width=\"91\" height=\"12\" /> dollars.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollars can buy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sodas leading us to a total of \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e19d2dd2b1cc8c21c6a728af3d9234062069713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+3=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> items. \nHence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8a806de3bdf2c155767a6042823fe88c689ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>- by interactivemath\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the two could by fractions of sandwiches, they'd be able to buy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/838493b7dbc5905e2494a7ad6253f21c9ed3eff2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30.00\\text{ dollars}}{4.50\\frac{\\text{dollars}}{\\text{sandwich}}}=6\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"147\" height=\"45\" /> sandwiches. But they can only buy a whole number of sandwiches, so they can buy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52d8fd11b9b621b42691bf89dddbe43bb730281a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot\\$4.50=\\$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"16\" />. So they have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/831d26f39684cd7cfa4ae5f2a0098b432dc8a6ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> left over, from which they can buy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> drinks (since they each cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/6739c8a3ef02d0f557bfbe01c9c92e562ff9a7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, for a total item count of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e19d2dd2b1cc8c21c6a728af3d9234062069713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+3=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> items. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-Elihemi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jo7ME7qg4Sg\">https://youtu.be/jo7ME7qg4Sg</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fy_IHyYru7s\">https://youtu.be/fy_IHyYru7s</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IgpayYB48C4?si=2nxxlhOYNmBnEhj5\">https://youtu.be/IgpayYB48C4?si=2nxxlhOYNmBnEhj5</a>\n~Math-X\n</p><p><br />\nThe Learning Royal: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IiFFDDITE6Q\">https://youtu.be/IiFFDDITE6Q</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution detailing how to solve the problem: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Puzy1HAlAKk&amp;list=PLbhMrFqoXXwmwbk2CWeYOYPRbGtmdPUhL&amp;index=2\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Puzy1HAlAKk&amp;list=PLbhMrFqoXXwmwbk2CWeYOYPRbGtmdPUhL&amp;index=2</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Y7wzKYaSOhI\">https://youtu.be/Y7wzKYaSOhI</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/WggTFT9FhNg\">https://youtu.be/WggTFT9FhNg</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic.281_to_25_Full_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span><span c